: 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [], "considered_alternatives": ["B2", "B3", "B4"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=100%, source=both]\n\nAdhesive Bowel Obstruction vs Chronic Constipation with Fecal Impaction:\n  Favours first:  abdominal distention, blood in stool, fever, green or yellow-green vomit, obstipation\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, confusion, constipation, frequent urination, inability to defecate\n\nAdhesive Bowel Obstruction vs Diabetic Neuropathy with Gastrointestinal Involvement:\n  Favours first:  abdominal distention, abdominal pain, blood in stool, dehydration, fever\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n\nAdhesive Bowel Obstruction vs Chronic Mesenteric Ischemia:\n  Favours first:  abdominal distention, abdominal pain, blood in stool, dehydration, diarrhea\n  Favours second: cold extremities, gangrene, hair loss on legs, intermittent claudication, ischemic rest pain\n\nAdhesive Bowel Obstruction vs Volvulus / Mechanical Bowel Obstruction:\n  Favours first:  abdominal distention, dehydration, obstipation, swollen firm belly\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abdominal cramping, dark-colored urine, firm abdomen, inability to pass gas\n\nChronic Constipation with Fecal Impaction vs Diabetic Neuropathy with Gastrointestinal Involvement:\n  Favours first:  abdominal bloating, abdominal pain, confusion, dehydration, frequent urination\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n\nChronic Constipation with Fecal Impaction vs Chronic Mesenteric Ischemia:\n  Favours first:  abdominal bloating, abdominal pain, confusion, constipation, dehydration\n  Favours second: cold extremities, gangrene, hair loss on legs, intermittent claudication, ischemic rest pain\n\nChronic Constipation with Fecal Impaction vs Volvulus / Mechanical Bowel Obstruction:\n  Favours first:  confusion, constipation, dehydration, frequent urination, inability to defecate\n  Favours second: abdominal cramping, blood in stool, dark-colored urine, fever, firm abdomen\n\nDiabetic Neuropathy with Gastrointestinal Involvement vs Chronic Mesenteric Ischemia:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n  Favours second: cold extremities, gangrene, hair loss on legs, intermittent claudication, ischemic rest pain\n\nDiabetic Neuropathy with Gastrointestinal Involvement vs Volvulus / Mechanical Bowel Obstruction:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abdominal cramping, abdominal pain, blood in stool, dark-colored urine\n\nChronic Mesenteric Ischemia vs Volvulus / Mechanical Bowel Obstruction:\n  Favours first:  cold extremities, gangrene, hair loss on legs, intermittent claudication, ischemic rest pain\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abdominal cramping, abdominal pain, blood in stool, dark-colored urine\n\nRelated to Diabetic Neuropathy with Gastrointestinal Involvement: diabetic autonomic neuropathy, diabetic polyneuropathy, peripheral neuropathy\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 55-year-old man presents to the emergency department with nausea and vomiting for the past week → feeding difficulties → Diabetic Neuropathy with Gastrointestinal Involvement"}
